          "title": "You'll want to know: l'impôt",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "l'impôt — \"a tax\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "impôt from Middle French impost from Medieval Latin impositum, \"a thing laid on\", from imponere (EtymDB 2.1) — a learned borrowing; the circumflex marks the s French later stopped writing."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
